  "reason": "Evidence: The two completed experiments (config_021, config_039) establish that multimodal + multiprofile + scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer achieves ~72.1-72.5% accuracy, with weighted fusion marginally preferred over concat. However, the RNA encoder choice (scvi_n200 vs scgpt) remains a major untested axis that could significantly shift performance. Question: config_007 tests scgpt as the RNA encoder while holding the other components at their best-known settings (imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion, multiprofile). This directly isolates the effect of a more specialized single-cell foundation model on the RNA side. Why this is the best next step: With 7 experiments remaining, resolving whether scgpt outperforms scvi_n200 is critical because it determines which RNA-encoder family to exploit in subsequent runs. If scgpt improves accuracy, it opens a promising sub-space (e.g., config_014, config_023); if not, we confirm scvi_n200 and pivot to image-encoder or aggregation variations. This single experiment reduces the largest remaining source of uncertainty in the design space."
